---

STEP 4: CREATE LAMBDA #1 IN THE PRODUCTION ACCOUNT

Open the AWS Console in the Production account.

Go to:

Lambda → Create function

Choose:
- Author from scratch
- Function name: start-retraining-lambda
- Runtime: Python 3.12 or Python 3.11
- Execution role: choose your existing Lambda role

After the function is created:
- go to Code
- choose Upload from → .zip file
- upload start_retraining_lambda.zip
- click Deploy

---

STEP 5: CREATE LAMBDA #2 IN THE PRODUCTION ACCOUNT

Still in the Production account:

Go to:

Lambda → Create function

Choose:
- Function name: register-model-version-lambda
- Runtime: Python 3.12 or Python 3.11
- Execution role: choose your existing Lambda role

Then:
- upload register_model_version_lambda.zip
- click Deploy

Now go to:

Configuration → Environment variables

Add this variable:

- Key: CONTROL_PLANE_ROLE_ARN
- Value: your Control Plane cross-account role ARN

Example:

arn:aws:iam::111111111111:role/CrossAccountModelRegistryRegistrationRole

That role is what Lambda #2 will assume before creating the new model version in Control Plane.

---

STEP 6: CREATE EVENTBRIDGE RULE #1 IN PRODUCTION

Go to:

Amazon EventBridge → Rules → Create rule

Set:

- Name: start-retrain-rule
- Event bus: default
- Rule type: Rule with an event pattern

For the event pattern, choose Custom pattern and paste:

~~~json
{
  "source": ["custom.mlops.retrain"],
  "detail-type": ["StartRetrain"]
}
~~~

For the target:
- choose Lambda function
- select start-retraining-lambda

Finish and create the rule.

This rule waits for your custom event and then starts the training job.

---

STEP 7: CREATE EVENTBRIDGE RULE #2 IN PRODUCTION

Go to:

Amazon EventBridge → Rules → Create rule

Set:

- Name: register-model-on-training-complete
- Event bus: default
- Rule type: Rule with an event pattern

Paste this event pattern:

~~~json
{
  "source": ["aws.sagemaker"],
  "detail-type": ["SageMaker Training Job State Change"],
  "detail": {
    "TrainingJobStatus": ["Completed"]
  }
}
~~~

For the target:
- choose Lambda function
- select register-model-version-lambda

Create the rule.

SageMaker sends SageMaker Training Job State Change events directly to EventBridge, so this rule is what wires training completion to registry update.

---

STEP 8: MAKE SURE EVENTBRIDGE CAN INVOKE THE LAMBDAS

Usually the console adds this automatically when you attach the Lambda as a target. If you use the console, you probably do not need to do anything else.

If you want to verify, open each Lambda and check:

Configuration → Permissions

You should see a resource-based policy allowing events.amazonaws.com to invoke it.

---

STEP 9: SEND THE EVENT THAT STARTS RETRAINING

Now you manually send the initial event into EventBridge in the Production account.

You can do this in CloudShell, terminal, or wherever AWS CLI is configured for the Production account.

Paste this into a file named event.json:

~~~json
[
  {
    "Source": "custom.mlops.retrain",
    "DetailType": "StartRetrain",
    "Detail": "{\"model_package_group_name\":\"credit-risk-model\",\"training_job_name\":\"prod-retrain-credit-risk-001\",\"training_image\":\"123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/my-train:latest\",\"inference_image\":\"123456789012.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/my-infer:latest\",\"role_arn\":\"arn:aws:iam::999999999999:role/SageMakerTrainingExecutionRole\",\"input_s3_uri\":\"s3://prod-ml-data/credit-risk/train/\",\"output_s3_uri\":\"s3://prod-ml-artifacts/credit-risk/retrain/\",\"instance_type\":\"ml.m5.xlarge\",\"approval_status\":\"Approved\",\"base_model_package_arn\":\"arn:aws:sagemaker:us-east-1:111111111111:model-package/credit-risk-model/5\",\"changed_feature_reason\":\"Updated production lookup column\"}"
  }
]
~~~

Then run:

~~~bash
aws events put-events --entries file://event.json
~~~

That should trigger Rule #1, which triggers Lambda #1, which starts the SageMaker training job.

